messages:
kai: Heads-up — I'm proposing a small TF refactor to our GPU pools so we can mix cheaper preemptible SKUs while still honoring pod-level latency with a fast fallback path. Draft plan below, please eyeball for gotchas.

maria: quick q — are we handling ENI / IP exhaustion for the denser instance types? last time we almost hit the limit with 100 nodes.

shawn: good call. we should limit pods-per-node via aws-node limits and use secondary ENIs + prefix-delegation where possible. also consider fewer smaller instances vs a couple huge ones.

kai: agree. plan is: (1) change ASG -> mixed instances policy with weighted instance_types, (2) add a small reserved on-demand pool (3-5 nodes) pinned to stable SKUs for low-latency requests, (3) spot pool with diversity + interruption handler and longer drain grace.

kai: Terraform snippet I'm testing:
```hcl
resource "aws_autoscaling_group" "gpu_mixed" {
  mixed_instances_policy {
    instances_distribution {
      on_demand_base_capacity = 5
      on_demand_percentage_above_base_capacity = 20
      spot_allocation_strategy = "capacity-optimized"
    }

    launch_template {
      launch_template_specification {
        launch_template_id = aws_launch_template.gpu_lt.id
        version = "$Latest"
      }

      overrides = [
        { instance_type = "g5.2xlarge", weighted_capacity = "8" },
        { instance_type = "g5.8xlarge", weighted_capacity = "32" },
        { instance_type = "g4dn.xlarge", weighted_capacity = "4" }
      ]
    }
  }
  lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }
  tags = [ { key = "cost_center", value = "infra-gpu", propagate_at_launch = true } ]
}
```

maria: looks reasonable. two notes: (a) weighted_capacity affects how ASG counts desired capacity — double-check our kube-scheduler resources mapping, (b) tag propagate_at_launch is crucial for billing and for k8s cloud provider tagging.

shawn: also add `instance_metadata_options { http_tokens = "required" }` to LT, and remove older AMI ids — rotate to the new gpu-optim AMI with ENA driver + nv_peer_mem.

julie: interruption handling: update our node-termination-handler config to extend drainGracePeriod to 240s for big-gpus and add a fallback label that triggers the fast on-demand pool. something like: `--drain-grace-period=240s --additional-pods-annotation=cluster-autoscaler.kubernetes.io/safe-to-evict`

kai: infra-bot ran `terraform plan` and flagged changes: 
```
~ aws_launch_template.gpu_lt: user_data will change (diff suppressed)
~ aws_autoscaling_group.gpu_mixed: replacing (forces new resource)
```

kai: risk: replacing ASG will momentarily remove spot capacity. mitigation: create new ASG beside old (create_before_destroy should help), and pre-scale new ASG to desired capacity before terminating old.

maria: regarding networking: run this to see current ENI headroom on the region before rollout:
`aws ec2 describe-network-interfaces --filters Name=availability-zone,Values=us-west-2a --query 'length(Reservations)'-not_exact_but_example`

shawn: also watch vCPU-based quotas for spot requests across instance families. smaller families might be unconstrained. put a quota check in the rollout doc.

kai: perf regressions: we'll add a quick e2e that hits the low-latency route (p95 < 120ms). if new instance mix breaks p95, rollback plan = scale down spot ASG to 0 and scale up pinned on-demand pool.

julie: tagging ask: add a `pool_type` tag = "spot-mixed" or "on-demand-stable" so billing and cost dashboards can split by route.

kai: one more Terraform snippet for tag policy:
```hcl
resource "aws_autoscaling_group" "gpu_mixed" {
  tags = [
    { key = "cost_center" , value = "infra-gpu", propagate_at_launch = true },
    { key = "pool_type" , value = "spot-mixed", propagate_at_launch = true }
  ]
}
```

infra-bot: CI check passed: `plan` succeeded; 2 resources to add, 1 to replace. No drift detected. :white_check_mark:

maria: ok from me if we add the ENI/quota checklist and the e2e gating. please add the checklist as a PR comment before merging.

shawn: i'll own the AMI rotation and run an early canary in one AZ tomorrow morning.

kai: thanks — opened PR #2184 with the changes and TODO checklist. merging after a green canary and ENI quota sign-off. :rocket:
